        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Levels vs Ascent comes down to what you are paying for. Levels gives you grass-fed, hormone-free dairy, a soy-free six-ingredient label and the lowest cost per gram on Amazon, about $1.43 per 25 g in the 5 lb tub. Ascent gives you Informed Sport certification on every batch, a mostly-isolate native whey with under 1 g of lactose, and a wider flavor range, for about $1.89 per 25 g on Amazon or less direct in the 4 lb size.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are not drug-tested and digest whey concentrate well, Levels is the better buy. If certification or lactose is the issue, choose Ascent. For more grass-fed options, including certified ones, start with our <a href="/best-grass-fed-whey-protein/">best grass-fed whey protein</a> rankings.
